{"name":"Flowering Reed","hex":"#e1d8b8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flowering","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of flower"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The period of time during which a plant is in flower.","The period of time during which someone or something is at its peak."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flowering"},{"term":"reed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various types of tall stiff perennial grass-like plants growing together in groups near water.","The hollow stem of these plants."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To thatch.","To mill or mint with reeding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg/500px-Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_47-_58_%281995%29._20210623_013709.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https: